            <ArticleTitle>Recent Advances in Therapeutic Endosonography for Cancer Treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>657-680</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1052-5157(17)30080-6</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.giec.2017.06.014</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Therapeutic endosonography (EUS) may play an important role in the management of cancers. EUS-guided fiducial placement has a high success rate and can aid in stereotactic radiotherapy. EUS-guided tumor ablation therapies can help in palliation of locally advanced tumors. EUS-guided antitumor injection seems to be feasible and safe in animals; initial human studies suffer from small sample size and lack of controls. Randomized, controlled trials have not shown benefit over conventional therapy. EUS celiac plexus neurolysis has gained popularity and is performed by interventional endosonographers. Large trials are needed to determine the most appropriate indications and overall usefulness of these therapies.</AbstractText>
